@startuml query-iterator-hierarchy
' The query-iterator family. These are iterator *adapters* (Rust has no class
' inheritance); the generalization arrows read as "specialises the base walk".
' All perform the lock-step A(W,k) ∩ D walk and yield Candidates; they differ in
' result ORDERING and in value-based FILTERING.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
  FontColor #102027
  AttributeFontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #1565C0

title Query-iterator family — same walk, different ordering & filtering

class "QueryIterator" as QI #BBDEFB {
  base lock-step DFS
  yields Candidate { term, distance }
}
class "StringQueryIterator" as SQ {
  yields owned String terms
}
class "OrderedQueryIterator" as OQ {
  distance-then-lexicographic
}
class "PriorityQueryIterator" as PQ {
  best-first by distance (heap)
}
class "ValueFilteredQueryIterator" as VF #C5CAE9 {
  prune by value predicate
}
class "ValueSetFilteredQueryIterator" as VSF #C5CAE9 {
  prune by value ∈ set
}
class "ValueYieldingQueryIterator" as VY #C5CAE9 {
  yields (term, distance, &value)
}

QI <|-- SQ
QI <|-- OQ
QI <|-- PQ
QI <|-- VF
VF <|-- VSF
QI <|-- VY

note bottom of VF
  Value-aware iterators require a MappedDictionary.
  Scope filtering here is the 10–100× speedup.
end note
@enduml
